\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Are there absolute $\epsilon _0,c_0>0$ such that for every $a,\rho >0$ with rho $a^3<\epsilon _0$, every thermodynamic sequence N,L$\to$infinity with $N/L^3\to \rho $, and every normalized bosonic hard-sphere ground eigenvector, the limiting lower condensate fraction is at least $c_0$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Are there absolute $\epsilon _0,c_0>0$ such that for every $a,\rho >0$ with rho $a^3<\epsilon _0$, every thermodynamic sequence N,L$\to$infinity with $N/L^3\to \rho $, and every normalized bosonic hard-sphere ground eigenvector, the limiting lower condensate fraction is at least $c_0$?

